A||N||19||Haze_Performance||I'm a bit ticked off with Fiero's!!!!  What a crappy day!!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-05-2001||12:42 AM||||Well I still have a timing problem with the 87 SE (V6)......And the engine mount gave out (FELL OUT) today in the 85 (L4)...... <BR>-------------------------------------------<P>The 87 just wont time!!!!!! The mark is 1" down on the crank..(Ive pulled the distributer out 100 times to try to get TDC) Im hearing a metal rubbing sound...I fear it might be a bearing..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> It could also be the waterpump. (I cant pinpoint it) Fierodave feels that its not the bearing. When I picked up the car from him the Alt. bolt was broke, so on start up it made lots of noise. He told me the rubbing noise I heard then was the Alt. Well the Alt. has been replaced and the noise is still there... The car stumbles on start up and just runs crappy at idle.. Im about to junk the whole car!!!! My health is not to good latly & this damn car is making me sicker. The only shop that I think the car will make it to wants to charge me over $200 to look at it.. I would hate to spend that much & have the guy tell me the bearing is bad.. If thats the case the car is going to be parted out.. <P>Is there any Illinois area Fiero mechanics that want to make a house call?? Ill be happy to pay you cash for a diagnosis & a little timing help. I do have a garage to work in & more tools than you can shake a stick at.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>  <P>I'm just a little stressed out & angry with fierodave right now. I was told that noise was something it wasn't  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I never would have bought this car if I would have known the engine was bad...<P><BR>I just feel stupid!!! I dont know why I cant get this car running?? Ive worked on cars for 20 years.. Rebuilding & Replacing engines, Trans work..... ect. This car has numbed my mind....<P><BR>Sorry but I had to vent..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I would be greatfull for advice you guys can give me.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||sqoach||03-05-2001||01:02 AM||||sorry to hear the trouble you're having. i can relate. but i won't bore you with my stories, cuz you've probably already heard them.<BR>well, i don't have any advice about the 87. sounds like you've tried as much as you can, or want to. i may be able to help you with the engine mount. which one is it? i'm pretty sure all of the mounts in my 85 parts' car are good if you need one. i also just changed out the dog-bone engine strut in my 86. only problem with the other one is that one of the rubber bushins was getting pretty worn. didn't bother just buying one of those (if you can).<P>wish i could help you out with your timing problem. good luck.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||03-05-2001||01:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>sorry to hear the trouble you're having. i can relate. but i won't bore you with my stories, cuz you've probably already heard them.<BR>well, i don't have any advice about the 87. sounds like you've tried as much as you can, or want to. i may be able to help you with the engine mount. which one is it? i'm pretty sure all of the mounts in my 85 parts' car are good if you need one. i also just changed out the dog-bone engine strut in my 86. only problem with the other one is that one of the rubber bushins was getting pretty worn. didn't bother just buying one of those (if you can).<P>wish i could help you out with your timing problem. good luck.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks sqoach.... I picked up all the new mounts today..Engine (2), Trans & Dogbone. Thats the only thing that went right today..<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Chance||03-05-2001||01:12 AM||||On the timing issue, did you look under the trunk lid and go by what it says? It seems to me they changed how/what it should be timed every 3rd Fiero off the line  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> as for metal rubbing sound...If you have a stethascope (or long enough vaccume tube) I would start it up, and check it out like that. I know what a pita it is to try everything you can and still get nowhere. I hope its not your T/O bearing in the tran||||reg||8
Z||000004||Ed||03-05-2001||01:15 AM||||Yeh, I've had days like that too.  <P>But, its just a car.  Just a chevy pushrod engine.  Walk away from it for a bit. If its really timing, what can be wrong?  The marks on the crank still there?  The distributor lined up in the right gear?  The timing chain not stretched or in the wrong tooth?  <P>As for the noise: Get out your stethoscope (or long screwdriver)and go for it.  Again, its just an engine.  Hope for the best, that is, a cheap bearing and not the cam or something.<P>But its just a car engine.   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MontanaFiero||03-05-2001||01:19 AM||||I don't know if this will help Haze, but it's worth a shot... I have had to replace two distributors because they were worn (chevy HEI distributors). Grab the shaft and see if there is any play in it. This could also cause your "bearing sound", and certainly prevent you from being able to time it. <P>Good Luck...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||03-05-2001||01:29 AM||||Well it will start & run. It just does not run well. I wast going to pick up a stethoscope in the morning. The timing mark is there (a little jumpie but there)Its about an inch down on the crank mark. I pulled the dis. and did the TDC thing, but it still wont line up. I even tried one tooth forward & one back to see if it would work...No luck. What should the RPM be at idle with a warmed up V6?<P><BR>Thanks guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
Z||000007||Greg Piet||03-05-2001||01:52 AM||||Fully warmed up it should be 900 RPM.<P>I had a similiar problem with the timing...<P>You already know some of this stuff but for those who dont.<P>Not all harmonic balancers have the proper timing marks.<BR>Remanufactured distributors for the Fiero in my experience are CRAP and cause timing woes.<BR>Diagnostic mode is kinda necessary in timing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>bad connections to the distributor can cause timing to not work effectively.<P>theres alays the timing chain stuff but lets not think about that.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Haze_Performance||03-05-2001||01:59 AM||||900 RPM Huh?? Thats where its at when warmed up, but it still wants to die..||||reg||11
Z||000009||Chance||03-05-2001||02:44 AM||||Oh, do you have it jumpered in Diagnostic mode?  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008694.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008694.html</A> ||||reg||14
