Z||000019||Turbo1dr||03-06-2001||06:40 AM||||Jumped timing chain? Check compression on all cylinders to see if they are low.<P>Have you checked to see if the computer is bad? Tap on it while it's running and note any RPM change or stutters.<P>Vacuum hoses routed correct? <P><BR>The noise is something to be heard before a correct diagnosis can be given most of the time.  Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Fiero (Buick Turbo V6 transplant in progress)<P><B>78 Malibu</B> 3.8L Turbo Buick<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Homex.html" TARGET=_blank>TURBO WONDER</A><BR>Best 8th: 1.548, 6.62@106.32  3450lb<BR>TE-70 3 bolt, Ported Stock Iron Heads and Intake<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Modifications_files/Intercooler.jpg" TARGET=_blank>2.5 stock intercoolers</A><BR>Vernon Swindell, Jr.||||reg||1
